n  readonly exclusion?: OverExclusionNode\n}\n\nexport interface OverBoundNode extends OperationNode {\n  readonly kind: 'OverBoundNode'\n  readonly type: OverBoundType\n  readonly value?: OperationNode\n}\n\nexport type OverBoundType =\n  | 'current row'\n  | 'unbounded preceding'\n  | 'preceding'\n  | 'unbounded following'\n  | 'following'\n\nexport interface OverExclusionNode extends OperationNode {\n  readonly kind: 'OverExclusionNode'\n  readonly type: 'current row' | 'group' | 'ties' | 'no others'\n}\n```\n\nActually, the upstream may have different field names. But this works.\n\nCompilation:\n```ts\nprotected override visitOver(node: OverNode): void {\n  this.append('over(')\n  if (node.partitionBy) { ... }\n  if (node.orderBy) { ... }\n  if (node.frame) {\n    this.append(' ')\n    this.visitNode(node.frame)\n  }\n  this.append(')')\n}\n\nprotected override visitOverFrame(node: OverFrameNode): void {\n  this.append(node.mode)\n  this.append(' ')\n  this.visitNode(node.start)\n  if (node.end) {\n    this.append(' and ')\n    this.visitNode(node.end)\n  }\n  if (node.exclusion) {\n    this.append(' exclude ')\n    this.append(node.exclusion.type)\n  }\n}\n\nprotected override visitOverBound(node: OverBoundNode): void {\n  if (node.value) {\n    this.visitNode(node.value)\n    this.append(' ')\n  }\n  this.append(node.type)\n}\n```\n\nWait, for `preceding(1)`, SQL is `1 preceding`, so value first then type. For `following(1)`, `1 following`. For `unbounded preceding`, just `unbounded preceding`. For `current row`, `current row`. So the bound compiler: if value present, append value + space, then type. Good.\n\nNow the OverNode transformer and visitor need the new node kinds and transforms.\n\nLet me also think about how `OverBuilder` methods add the frame. The `rows/range/groups` methods take a callback receiving an `OverFrameBuilder`. The builder needs mode set. So `rows` creates `new OverFrameBuilder({ mode: 'rows' })`, `range` -> mode 'range', `groups` -> mode 'groups'.\n\nThe frame builder props:\n```ts\ninterface OverFrameBuilderProps {\n  readonly mode: OverFrameMode\n  readonly overFrameNode?: OverFrameNode\n}\n```\n\nActually I'll design like:\n- `OverFrameBuilder` holds `mode` and `overFrameNode` (the node built so far).\n- Single bound methods create `OverFrameExclusionBuilder` with a new node.\n- Two-sided starter methods create `OverFrameTwoSidedStartBuilder` with a node containing start.\n- `OverFrameTwoSidedStartBuilder.and*` creates `OverFrameExclusionBuilder` with node containing start+end.\n- `OverFrameExclusionBuilder` has `exclude*` methods that set exclusion and return a new `OverFrameExclusionBuilder` (or itself). It also has `toOperationNode()`.\n\nBut what does `rows(cb)` do with the result? It calls `cb(new OverFrameBuilder({ mode: 'rows' }))`, gets back an `OverFrameExclusionBuilder` (or maybe `OverFrameBuilder` if user returns something weird). Then calls `.toOperationNode()` and sets it on OverNode with mode 'rows'.\n\nHowever, if the callback returns an `OverFrameBuilder` that hasn't called any bound method, there's no node. We can type the callback to return `OverFrameExclusionBuilder<DB,TB>`.\n\nLet me now think about the actual upstream types. I want to match the Kysely public API closely so that typings tests would pass. Since we don't have access to upstream tests, but the task spec is detailed enough. Let me reconstruct from what I remember of Kysely 0.29's `over-builder.ts`:\n\nActually, I recall the Kysely 0.29 over-builder.ts API:\n```ts\nexport class OverBuilder<DB, TB extends keyof DB>\n  implements OrderByInterface<DB, TB, {}>, OperationNodeSource\n{\n  ...\n  /**\n   * Adds a `rows` frame to the `over` function.\n   */\n  rows<OFB extends OverFrameBuilder<DB, TB>>(\n    cb: (overFrameBuilder: OverFrameBuilder<DB, TB>) => OFB,\n  ): OverBuilder<DB, TB>\n\n  range<OFB extends OverFrameBuilder<DB, TB>>(cb: ...): OverBuilder<DB, TB>\n\n  groups<OFB extends OverFrameBuilder<DB, TB>>(cb: ...): OverBuilder<DB, TB>\n}\n```\n\nAnd in over-frame-builder.ts:\n```ts\nexport class OverFrameBuilder<DB, TB extends keyof DB> {\n  readonly #props: OverFrameBuilderProps\n\n  constructor(props: OverFrameBuilderProps) {\n    this.#props = freeze(props)\n  }\n\n  betweenUnboundedPreceding(): OverFrameTwoSidedStartBuilder<DB, TB> {\n    return new OverFrameTwoSidedStartBuilder({\n      ...this.#props,\n      overFrameNode: OverFrameNode.create(this.#props.mode, {\n        type: 'unbounded preceding',\n      }),\n    })\n  }\n  ...\n}\n\nexport class OverFrameTwoSidedStartBuilder<DB, TB> {\n  ...\n  andCurrentRow(): OverFrameExclusionBuilder<DB, TB> {\n    return new OverFrameExclusionBuilder({\n      ...this.#props,\n      overFrameNode: OverFrameNode.cloneWithEnd(this.#props.overFrameNode, {\n        type: 'current row',\n      }),\n    })\n  }\n}\n\nexport class OverFrameExclusionBuilder<DB, TB> implements OperationNodeSource {\n  ...\n  excludeCurrentRow(): OverFrameExclusionBuilder<DB, TB> {\n    return new OverFrameExclusionBuilder({\n      ...this.#props,\n      overFrameNode: OverFrameNode.cloneWithExclusion(this.#props.overFrameNode, {\n        type: 'current row',\n      }),\n    })\n  }\n  ...\n  toOperationNode(): OverFrameNode {\n    return this.#props.overFrameNode\n  }\n}\n```\n\nNow for value expressions, the builder methods accept `number | bigint | Expression<any>`:\n```ts\npreceding(offset: number | bigint | Expression<any>): OverFrameExclusionBuilder<DB, TB>\n```\n\nAnd they parse using `parseValueExpression(offset)`. But `parseValueExpression` accepts `ValueExpression<any, any, unknown>`, which is `V | ExpressionOrFactory<DB,TB,V>`. For `Expression<any>`, that works. For `number | bigint`, ValueNode.create. Good.\n\nNow I need to add the new node files:\n- `over-frame-node.ts`\n- `over-bound-node.ts`\n- `over-exclusion-node.ts`\n- `group-by-grouping-node.ts`\n\nAnd add to operation-node.ts kinds, operation-node-visitor.ts, operation-node-trans